# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. This repo is public. Nothing in this block may ever be committed.
# (create-next-app overwrote this file once already — if you re-scaffold,
#  check this block survived before you run `git add`.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.docx
*.doc
.~*
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*secret*
!scripts/check-secrets.mjs
*credential*
*API*Key*

# Legacy recorded model replies may contain prompts; never commit them.
course/cafe/fixtures.*.json
course/progress.json
legacy/course-python/cafe/fixtures.*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.next/
/out/
/build
/coverage
/output/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/.playwright-cli/
/blob-report/
/browser-evidence/
/.playwright-raw/
/.playwright-private/
/.playwright-evidence-contract-safe/
/.playwright-evidence-contract-private/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# Python virtualenvs, anywhere in the tree
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local dev tooling
.claude/

# Course 10 MCP rights-review and raw-capture workspaces. These contain
# non-public source candidates or privacy-bearing window chrome and must never
# be swept into the public repository by `git add -A`.
/tmp/mcp-rights-hold/
/tmp/mcp-ui-evidence/

# Private working notes. Untracked is not enough: `git add -A` would stage
# these into a public repo.
2026*_claude suggestions*.md

# Junk
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nested dependency trees. `/node_modules` above is root-anchored and does not
# reach video-pilot/agent-loop-120s/node_modules — 8,002 files that `git add -A`
# would sweep into this public repo. Reinstallable from their own lockfiles.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# Course review workspace: 621 MB, 3,803 PNGs of review evidence. Kept on disk,
# never committed — git does not forget a blob once it is in history.
/course_review_2026-08-23/

# Separate HyperFrames project with its own AGENTS.md and lockfile: 906 MB,
# 563 MB of it uncompressed .wav. Nothing in this repo references it — the only
# tracked mentions are this file and eslint.config.mjs, both of which exclude
# it. It belongs in its own repository, not in every clone of this one.
/video-pilot/

# Third-party PDFs pulled in for research. Redistributing them from a public
# repo is a rights question nobody has answered; tmp/ itself stays because the
# course release checkers read from it.
/tmp/pdfs/
